---
name: "Build Task"
description: "Implements a single build task"
tags: [build]
stage: build
---
Read the current Mohist issue details before interpreting this task:

```bash
mo issue view ${{ issue.number }} --project ${{ issue.projectId }}
```

<artifact id="build-task">

<task>
Complete exactly one implementation task from `tasks.json`.
Deliver the complete feature slice described by the task.
A task may span multiple files and include both implementation and its prerequisites (refactoring, interface definition, DI wiring) as well as relevant tests.
</task>

<dependencies>
Read the context files before implementing:
- `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/proposal.md`
- `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/design.md`
- `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/tasks.json`
- relevant specs under `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/specs/`
- `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/progress.txt` if it exists — prior tasks' recorded
  decisions, gotchas, and established patterns. Read the `## Codebase Patterns`
  section first.
</dependencies>

<instruction>
Follow the selected task description and acceptance criteria.

If the task references a spec requirement:
1. Read the referenced spec file.
2. Locate the requirement section.
3. Ensure every WHEN/THEN scenario in that requirement passes.
4. Treat acceptance criteria as supplementary checks.

If the task has no spec reference, treat its acceptance criteria as the complete verification list.
</instruction>

<implementation_policy>
- Implement the complete feature slice described in the task.
- Include necessary refactoring, interface changes, and wiring as part of this task.
- Follow repository conventions.
- Avoid unrelated refactors.
- Preserve existing behavior unless the task explicitly changes it.
- You may be interrupted at any time: commit incrementally and keep your progress
  notes current.
- Commit your changes on the workflow's per-run branch (`${{ workspace.branch }}`).
  This branch is prepared by the runner and is the source ref used by
  the Integrate stage. Do not switch to or create a different worktree-style
  branch such as `mo/issue-${{ issue.number }}`; all task, check, repair,
  merge, and conflict-resolver work must run inside the workflow workspace
  at `${{ workspace.path }}` and stay on `${{ workspace.branch }}`.
</implementation_policy>

<verification>
Run typecheck, tests, or focused verification appropriate for the changed area.
If this task involves refactoring existing code:
1. First run the existing tests that cover the refactored area
2. Confirm they pass before proceeding with new implementation
3. This regression check is part of this task, not a separate task

Write or update tests as part of this task. Every task must include relevant test coverage.
All acceptance criteria must pass before reporting completion.
</verification>

<progress_tracking>
`openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/progress.txt` is this issue's working memory.
Record noteworthy discoveries as you work — patterns, decisions, gotchas,
anything that might help later steps. Don't think about structure — just append.
Before finishing, review and make sure your key learnings are recorded.
</progress_tracking>

<completion>
When you have completed all work for this task, stage and commit your changes,
including your `openspec/changes/issue-${{ issue.number }}/progress.txt` entry. The commit message
should start with the task ID.

Output `<promise>done</promise>` at the end of your response when complete.
If you have NOT completed the task, output `<promise>unfinished</promise>` instead.
</completion>

</artifact>
